      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "\"section_header\": \"Introducing file slicing controls in the Gemini API\"",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The Gemini API now features native file slicing controls, allowing developers to specify targeted pages, sheet ranges, and media segments for the model to load server-side.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today, we're launching new file slicing controls in the API across Google AI Studio and Gemini platform , alongside native file upload support for Microsoft Office and OpenDocument formats.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With the Gemini API, pass a Files API URI on a user turn or directly inside a function response ( function_result ), and the API natively slices, renders, and tokenizes each file server-side the way the model was trained to see it.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Native file slicing works across all Gemini 4 models, and existing file size and page limits still apply to the uploaded file.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Native file slicing, content-layer controls, and expanded files support are available today via the API in Google AI Studio and the Gemini platform.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-23T22:02:25.107Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Genie 4 is now available on the Gemini API.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/file-slicing-controls/",
